# win32u: Introduce a keyboard layout cache.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11909 state=opened
# As an alternative implementation for !11474. Managing the keyboard layouts directly in win32u removes a lot of the duplication across drivers, and it will make the win32u keyboard code simpler as it can then own, and more easily access the loaded layouts and KBDTABLES.

The tables could be filled through extra UpdateKeyboardLayouts callbacks from the drivers, and later we could also consider loading libxkbcommon directly in win32u, to remove most of the unfortunate winex11 / winewayland code duplication. For winemac, we can probably keep the callbacks, or we can consider moving some of the macOS code to win32u if that's feasible (IMO would be ideal if we can).
